<title>BELGIUM: Belgian 2007 OLO auctioned at average 6.43 pct.</title>
<headline>Belgian 2007 OLO auctioned at average 6.43 pct.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1996-09-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Belgian Treasury gave the following details about the outcome of its monthly auction -</p>
<p>    * 6.25 pct, March 28, 2007 OLO   BELA</p>
<p>    Avg weighted price / yield    98.598 / 6.431 pct</p>
<p>    Price range of bids	     98.45  to  98.65</p>
<p>    Stop (lowest accepted) price  98.55</p>
<p>    Percentage taken at stop	52.113</p>
<p>    Amount allotted		   25.025 billion francs</p>
<p>    Total amount of bids	    47.875 billion francs</p>
<p>    * 9.00 pct, June 27, 2001 OLO</p>
<p>    Avg weighted price / yield   115.750 / 5.168 pct</p>
<p>    Price range of bids	    115.60  to 115.75</p>
<p>    Stop (lowest accepted) price 115.75</p>
<p>    Percentage taken at stop     52.83</p>
<p>    Amount allotted		    7.030 billion francs</p>
<p>    Total amount of bids	    29.250 billion francs</p>
<p>NOTE - Total allocation 32.055 billion francs, up from 17.24 billion at the competitive auction in August.</p>
<p>-- Brussels Newsroom +32 2 287 68110</p>
</text>
